.TH YOUTUI 1 "2026-07-17" "1.0.4" "Youtui Manual"
.SH NAME
youtui \- Terminal user interface for YouTube Music
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B youtui
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] [\fI\,URL\/\fR] [\fI\,COMMAND\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Youtui is a text-based user interface for browsing, searching, and playing
music from YouTube Music. It supports album splitting, metadata enrichment,
Last.fm scrobbling, lyrics display, and playlist management.

When run without a subcommand, Youtui launches the full TUI. Subcommands
provide CLI utilities for debugging, cache management, and authentication.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B (none)
Run the TUI. This is the default when no subcommand is given. Requires a
valid cookie file for YouTube Music authentication.
.TP
.B scrobble-cache
Inspect or manage the offline scrobble cache. Failed scrobbles are queued
here for background retry.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-show
List cached entries with retry counts (default if no flags given).
.TP
.B \-\-clear
Remove all cached entries.
.TP
.B \-\-retry
Force immediate retry of all cached scrobbles.
.RE
.TP
.B metadata-cache
Inspect or manage the SQLite metadata cache.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-show
List all cached metadata entries (default if no flags given).
.TP
.B \-\-clear
Delete all cached entries.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Show cache statistics: entry count and database file size.
.RE
.TP
.B logs
Inspect or manage application log files.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-show
Print the last N lines from the newest log file (default if no flags).
.TP
.B \-\-follow
Tail the newest log file in real time.
.TP
.B \-\-clear
Truncate all log files.
.TP
.B \-\-count \fI\,N\/\fR
Number of lines to show (default 50).
.RE
.TP
.B test-scrobble
Submit a test scrobble to Last.fm. Requires the [scrobbling] config section.
.RS
.TP
.I ARTIST
Artist name.
.TP
.I TRACK
Track title.
.TP
.I ALBUM
Optional album name.
.TP
.I DURATION
Duration in seconds (default 240).
.RE
.TP
.B test-validate-metadata
Run the metadata pipeline for a given artist and title. Queries Last.fm,
MusicBrainz, Discogs, and other providers. Prints resolved album info and
track listing.
.RS
.TP
.I ARTIST
Artist name.
.TP
.I TITLE
Track title.
.TP
.I ALBUM
Optional album name hint.
.RE
.TP
.B test-listenbrainz
Test the ListenBrainz metadata provider with a specific artist and title.
.RS
.TP
.I ARTIST
Artist name.
.TP
.I TITLE
Track title.
.TP
.B \-\-release \fI\,RELEASE\/\fR
Optional release name hint.
.RE
.TP
.B auth-musicbrainz
Interactive MusicBrainz OAuth2 setup. Prints an authorization URL, then
exchanges the code for a bearer token and saves it to the config file.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-code \fI\,CODE\/\fR
OAuth2 authorization code from the browser redirect. If omitted, prints
the URL to open and instructions.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-debug
Display and log additional debug information.
.TP
.B \-\-disable-media-controls
Disable system media control integration (MPRIS).
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-show-source
Print raw JSON from the YouTube Music API instead of processed output.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-input-json \fI\,PATH\/\fR
Process local JSON file(s) as if received from the API. Can be passed
multiple times for endpoints that support continuations.
.TP
.B \-\-auth-type \fI\,TYPE\/\fR
Force a specific authentication type (browser, oauth).
.TP
.B \-D, \-\-downloader-type \fI\,TYPE\/\fR
Force a specific downloader type (yt-dlp, ffmpeg).
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Skip duplicate check when adding a URL.
.TP
.B \-\-generate-completions \fI\,SHELL\/\fR
Generate shell completion script for bash, zsh, fish, or PowerShell.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B YT_COOKIE
Path to the Netscape-format cookies.txt file for YouTube Music
authentication. Overrides the default location.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/youtui/config.toml
Main configuration file. Contains auth settings, scrobbling credentials,
keybindings, and UI preferences.
.TP
.B ~/.config/youtui/cookie.txt
Netscape-format cookie file for YouTube Music authentication.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/youtui/metadata_cache.sqlite
SQLite database caching metadata from Last.fm, MusicBrainz, Discogs, and
other providers.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/youtui/scrobble_cache.json
JSON file storing failed scrobbles for background retry.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/youtui/debug*.log
Rotating debug log files. The newest file has the highest number.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run the TUI
youtui
.TP
Run with debug logging
youtui \-\-debug
.TP
Show failed scrobbles
youtui scrobble-cache
.TP
Clear scrobble cache
youtui scrobble-cache \-\-clear
.TP
Retry failed scrobbles now
youtui scrobble-cache \-\-retry
.TP
Show metadata cache stats
youtui metadata-cache \-\-stats
.TP
Clear metadata cache
youtui metadata-cache \-\-clear
.TP
View last 100 log lines
youtui logs \-\-count 100
.TP
Follow logs in real time
youtui logs \-\-follow
.TP
Clear all log files
youtui logs \-\-clear
.TP
Test a scrobble
youtui test-scrobble "Radiohead" "Creep" "Pablo Honey" 239
.TP
Test metadata pipeline
youtui test-validate-metadata "The Beatles" "Yesterday" "Help!"
.TP
Test ListenBrainz lookup
youtui test-listenbrainz "Aphex Twin" "Windowlicker" \-\-release "Windowlicker"
.TP
Start MusicBrainz OAuth
youtui auth-musicbrainz
.TP
Complete MusicBrainz OAuth
youtui auth-musicbrainz \-\-code "YOUR_CODE_HERE"
.SH EXIT STATUS
.IP 0
Success.
.IP 1
Error (invalid arguments, network failure, authentication failure, or
internal error).
